course: dictionary
lesson: 11563
title: Words about body shape
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Anatomically looks long, but its root helps. Anatomy is the study of how the parts of a living thing are built and fit together. The ending -ally turns it into an adverb, so it tells you how something is done or shown.
explain: «The model of the heart is anatomically correct.» The clue is correct: the model is built like a real heart, with the same parts in the same places. So anatomically must be about the body's structure.
explain: Check with the swap test. «The drawing is anatomically correct» can become «The drawing shows the body's structure correctly.» It still makes sense, so your meaning works.
fact: Anatomically means in a way that is to do with the structure of the body.
fact: Anatomy is the study of how the parts of a body are built and how they fit together.
fact: Anatomically is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done, shown or drawn.
fact: «Anatomically similar» means the parts have a similar shape and arrangement.
fact: Scientists use models and drawings that are anatomically correct to learn how the body works.
exercise: «The toy skeleton is anatomically correct, with bones in the right places.» What does anatomically mean here? | In a way that is very fast | In a way that makes a loud sound | *In a way that matches the body's structure | In a way that is painted bright colours
exercise: «The two drawings are anatomically similar.» What does anatomically similar mean? | They were drawn on the same day | They are both very big | They are the same colour | *They have the same body structure and shape
exercise: «The teacher showed the heart anatomically.» Find and copy the word that tells you how the heart was shown. | *anatomically | showed | teacher | heart
test: «The model is anatomically correct, so it shows where each organ sits.» What does anatomically correct mean? | Painted in bright colours | Made of wood | *Right about the way the body is built | Very small and light
test: What is the best meaning of anatomically? | To do with the weather | To do with speed | To do with money | *To do with the structure of the body
exam: Ella reads «The diagram is anatomically similar to a real hand.» What does anatomically mean? | To do with the sea | *To do with the structure of the body | To do with colour | To do with sound
